{"description": "Extracts text elements from every new or changed document in the RAG inventory through the rag_core extractor registry; corrupt documents are marked failed without failing the flow.", "displayName": "RAG - Extract Text.step", "flowMetadata": {"inputPorts": [{"name": "_rgex_inventory", "displayName": "_rgex_inventory", "minEntries": 1, "maxEntries": 1, "type": "table", "id": "_rgex_inventory", "label": "_rgex_inventory"}], "outputPorts": [{"name": "_rgex_invout", "displayName": "_rgex_invout", "minEntries": 1, "maxEntries": 1, "columnDelta": null, "type": "table"}]}, "metadataVersion": 1, "name": "RAG - Extract Text.step", "properties": {}, "templates": {"SAS": "/******************************************************************************\n * Copyright \u00a9 2026, SAS Institute Inc., Cary, NC, USA.  All Rights Reserved.\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * RAG - Extract Text: re-read every new/changed document from the inventory\n * and extract text elements through the rag_core extractor registry into the\n * promoted CAS table <project>_ELEMENTS (varchar - no 32k limit). A corrupt\n * document is marked failed in the inventory and never fails the flow.\n * Thin shell over rag_core.steps.run_extract - see the About tab.\n ******************************************************************************/\n%macro _rgex_setup;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgex_ragProject) %then %global _rgex_ragProject;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgex_tablesCaslib) %then %global _rgex_tablesCaslib;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgex_persist) %then %global _rgex_persist;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgex_persist)) EQ 0 %then %let _rgex_persist = 1;\n%mend _rgex_setup;\n%_rgex_setup;\n/* Pipeline-wide state, shared by every RAG step in this session.\n   RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR: 1 (default) stops a SAS Studio Flow at the failing\n   step, which is what an interactive user wants. A SCHEDULED run sets it to\n   0: an aborted session never sends SAS Job Execution its completion\n   handshake, so the job would report running forever and its dead compute\n   server would keep counting against the context's server limit.\n   RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED: set by the step that fails; later steps then skip\n   their work and pass the inventory through, so the flow finishes tidily\n   instead of loading half a corpus. */\n%macro _rag_pipeline_state;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR) %then %do;\n        %global RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR;\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR = 1;\n    %if not %symexist(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED) %then %global RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED;\n    %if %length(%superq(RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 0;\n%mend _rag_pipeline_state;\n%_rag_pipeline_state;\n\n%let _rgex_viyaHost = %sysfunc(getoption(SERVICESBASEURL));\n%let _rgex_rc = 1;\n%let _rgex_state = run;\n%let _rgex_error = The Python program did not run.;\n%let _rgex_summary = ;\n%let _rgex_nel = 0;\n%let _rgex_ninv = 0;\n\n%macro _rgex_guard;\n    %if &RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED. NE 0 %then %do;\n        %let _rgex_state = skip;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: RAG - Extract Text: skipped - an earlier step of this run failed\";\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgex_guard;\n%_rgex_guard;\n%macro _rgex_inherit;\n    %global _rgex_runId;\n    %local dsid vproject vcaslib vrun rc;\n    %if %symexist(_rgex_inventory) %then\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgex_inventory)) NE 0 %then %do;\n        %if %sysfunc(exist(&_rgex_inventory.)) %then %do;\n            %let dsid = %sysfunc(open(&_rgex_inventory., i));\n            %if &dsid. NE 0 %then %do;\n                %let vproject = %sysfunc(varnum(&dsid., rag_project));\n                %let vcaslib = %sysfunc(varnum(&dsid., tables_caslib));\n                %let vrun = %sysfunc(varnum(&dsid., run_id));\n                %if %sysfunc(fetch(&dsid.)) EQ 0 %then %do;\n                    %if &vproject. GT 0 %then\n                        %let _rgex_ragProject = %sysfunc(getvarc(&dsid., &vproject.));\n                    %if &vcaslib. GT 0 %then\n                        %let _rgex_tablesCaslib = %sysfunc(getvarc(&dsid., &vcaslib.));\n                    /* the run id too: the lock belongs to the RUN, so a step\n                       that fails has to know which lock row to hand back */\n                    %if &vrun. GT 0 %then\n                        %let _rgex_runId = %sysfunc(getvarc(&dsid., &vrun.));\n                %end;\n                %let rc = %sysfunc(close(&dsid.));\n            %end;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n    /* a missing project is a failure of THIS step - but not when the step is\n       already skipping, where an absent inventory is expected */\n    %if &_rgex_state. EQ run %then\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgex_ragProject)) EQ 0 %then %do;\n        %let _rgex_state = fail;\n        /* one line: the value is embedded in a quoted putLog below, so a\n           newline inside it would break the string */\n        %let _rgex_error = the inventory does not name a RAG project - wire the output of RAG - List Documents into this step;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgex_tablesCaslib)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let _rgex_tablesCaslib = casuser;\n%mend _rgex_inherit;\n%_rgex_inherit;\n%macro _rgex_port_default;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgex_invout) %then %global _rgex_invout;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgex_invout)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let _rgex_invout = rgexout.&_rgex_ragProject._INV_EXTRACT;\n%mend _rgex_port_default;\n%_rgex_port_default;\n/* One CAS session for the whole step: created here, reused by\n   SWAT inside proc python, promote+save done by proc casutil.\n   rgexout is where the step's OUTPUT TABLE lands by default -\n   the same caslib as the pipeline tables, so a flow leaves its\n   intermediate results next to each other. */\ncas rgexcas uuidmac=_rgex_casuuid;\n%let _rgex_cashost = %sysfunc(getoption(CASHOST));\n%let _rgex_casport = %sysfunc(getoption(CASPORT));\nlibname rgexout cas caslib=\"&_rgex_tablesCaslib.\" sessref=rgexcas;\n\n%macro _rgex_export(portvar, file);\n    %if %symexist(&portvar.) %then %do;\n        %if %length(%superq(&&portvar.)) GT 0 %then %do;\n            %if %sysfunc(exist(&&&portvar..)) %then %do;\n                filename _rgex_io \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/&file.\";\n                proc json out=_rgex_io noSASTags;\n                    export &&&portvar..;\n                run; quit;\n                filename _rgex_io clear;\n            %end;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgex_export;\n%_rgex_export(_rgex_inventory, rgex_inventory_in.json);\n\nproc python restart;\nsubmit;\ndef main():\n    import json\n    import os\n    import sys\n    import tempfile\n    import time\n    import traceback\n\n    # nothing to do when the step is only passing the inventory through\n    if str(SAS.symget(\"_rgex_state\") or \"run\").strip() != \"run\":\n        return\n\n    def sas_safe(text):\n        \"\"\"Strings crossing into SAS.logMessage/SAS.symput are embedded into\n        generated SAS statements - quotes and macro characters corrupt the\n        code stream (verified live). EVERY such string goes through here.\"\"\"\n        cleaned = str(text)\n        for ch in (\"'\", '\"', \"%\", \"&\", \";\"):\n            cleaned = cleaned.replace(ch, \" \")\n        return cleaned\n\n    def M(msg):\n        SAS.logMessage(\"RAGEXTRACT \" + sas_safe(msg))\n\n    try:\n        import requests\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the requests package - see \"\n                                   \"the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n    try:\n        import pandas as pd\n        import swat\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the swat/pandas packages \"\n                                   \"required for the CAS table transport - \"\n                                   \"see the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n\n    BASE = str(SAS.symget(\"_rgex_viyaHost\") or \"\").rstrip(\"/\")\n    TOKEN = os.environ.get(\"SAS_SERVICES_TOKEN\", \"\")\n    AUTH = {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN}\n    VERIFY = os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\") or os.environ.get(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\") or True\n    WORKPATH = SAS.workpath if SAS.workpath.endswith(os.sep) else SAS.workpath + os.sep\n\n    P = {name: str(SAS.symget(name) or \"\").strip() for name in [\n        \"_rgex_extractor\",\n        \"_rgex_ragProject\",\n        \"_rgex_tablesCaslib\",\n        \"_rgex_ragCorePath\",\n    ]}\n\n    def read_rows(filename, missing_message):\n        path = WORKPATH + filename\n        if not os.path.exists(path):\n            raise RuntimeError(missing_message)\n        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            data = json.load(fh)\n        rows = []\n        for row in data if isinstance(data, list) else []:\n            rows.append({str(k).lower(): v for k, v in row.items()})\n        return rows\n\n    def multiline(control):\n        \"\"\"Every line a user typed into a multi-line text field.\n\n        SAS Studio splits such a field for us: it emits <control>_count and\n        <control>_1..N, and leaves the plain macro variable holding only the\n        FIRST line. Reading just the plain one silently turned two questions\n        into one run-on question (found live in a flow). Semicolons are still\n        accepted, for callers that set the parameter directly.\n        \"\"\"\n        values = []\n        try:\n            count = int(float(SAS.symget(control + \"_count\") or 0))\n        except Exception:\n            count = 0\n        if count > 0:\n            for index in range(1, count + 1):\n                try:\n                    piece = str(SAS.symget(\"%s_%d\" % (control, index)) or \"\")\n                except Exception:\n                    piece = \"\"\n                if piece.strip():\n                    values.append(piece.strip())\n            if values:\n                return values\n        raw = str(P.get(control) or \"\").replace(\";\", \"\\n\")\n        return [line.strip() for line in raw.split(\"\\n\") if line.strip()]\n\n    def clean_path(raw):\n        \"\"\"Path-selector values arrive scheme-prefixed (sasserver:/...,\n        sascontent:/...); strip the scheme off.\"\"\"\n        value = str(raw or \"\").strip()\n        for scheme in (\"sascontent:\", \"sasserver:\"):\n            if value.lower().startswith(scheme):\n                return value[len(scheme):]\n        return value\n\n    STARTED = time.time()\n    SUMMARY = []\n\n    def summarize(line):\n        \"\"\"One line of the step's log summary (SAS prints them at the end).\"\"\"\n        SUMMARY.append(str(line))\n\n    def publish_summary(target):\n        elapsed = time.time() - STARTED\n        summarize(f\"elapsed {elapsed:.1f}s\")\n        SAS.symput(target, sas_safe(\" | \".join(SUMMARY))[:1500])\n\n    def write_rows(filename, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n        out = []\n        for row in rows:\n            rec = {}\n            for column in columns:\n                value = row.get(column)\n                if column in numeric:\n                    try:\n                        rec[column] = float(value or 0)\n                    except Exception:\n                        rec[column] = 0.0\n                else:\n                    rec[column] = \"\" if value is None else str(value)\n            out.append(rec)\n        with open(WORKPATH + filename, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            json.dump(out, fh)\n        return len(out)\n\n    try:\n        # ---- CAS: reuse the session the step created in SAS ---------------\n        # (sas-studio-custom-steps: Reuse-CAS-session-from-SWAT)\n        import re as _re\n        os.environ.setdefault(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\",\n                              os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\", \"\"))\n        try:\n            conn = swat.CAS(hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgex_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                            port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgex_casport\") or 5570)),\n                            password=TOKEN,\n                            session=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgex_casuuid\") or \"\"))\n        except Exception as exc:\n            # The step reuses the CAS session SAS created, because the staged\n            # table has to be visible to the casutil promote that follows. CAS\n            # only lets an identity reconnect to its OWN session, and a context\n            # that runs the server as a service account breaks that: SAS and\n            # its token are the service account while the CAS session belongs\n            # to the user who launched the job.\n            #\n            # SWAT's exception says only \"Could not connect ... on port 5570\";\n            # the server's real message (\"Users can only reconnect to their own\n            # sessions\") goes to stderr and never reaches the exception, so\n            # matching on text does not work. Connecting WITHOUT the session id\n            # separates the two causes: if that works, CAS is reachable and the\n            # problem is whose session it is.\n            reachable = False\n            try:\n                probe = swat.CAS(\n                    hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgex_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                    port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgex_casport\") or 5570)),\n                    password=TOKEN)\n                reachable = True\n                probe.close()\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n            if reachable:\n                raise RuntimeError(\n                    \"this compute context cannot run the RAG steps: CAS is \"\n                    \"reachable, but the SAS session and the CAS session belong \"\n                    \"to different identities, so the step cannot reuse the CAS \"\n                    \"session it needs. The stock 'SAS Job Execution compute \"\n                    \"context' has this problem because it runs the server as a \"\n                    \"service account. Run the job in a context that runs as the \"\n                    \"REQUESTING USER - the 'SAS Studio compute context' does, \"\n                    \"and a full flow was verified there. See the RAG \"\n                    \"administration guide.\")\n            raise\n        CASLIB = P[\"_rgex_tablesCaslib\"] or \"casuser\"\n        if not _re.match(r\"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,19}$\",\n                         P[\"_rgex_ragProject\"] or \"\"):\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                \"ragProject must be 1-20 characters (letters, digits, \"\n                \"underscores, starting with a letter) so every \"\n                \"project_suffix table name stays within the 32 characters \"\n                \"SAS Studio displays\")\n\n        def project_table(suffix):\n            return P[\"_rgex_ragProject\"] + suffix\n\n        def stamp(rows):\n            \"\"\"Every inventory row names its pipeline, so the next step\n            inherits the project and caslib instead of asking again.\"\"\"\n            for row in rows:\n                row[\"rag_project\"] = P[\"_rgex_ragProject\"]\n                row[\"tables_caslib\"] = CASLIB\n            return rows\n\n        def cas_read(name, required_message=None):\n            \"\"\"Read a pipeline table into lower-cased row dicts; absent\n            table = empty (the pipeline's empty state) unless required.\"\"\"\n            if not conn.table.tableExists(caslib=CASLIB, name=name).exists:\n                if required_message:\n                    raise RuntimeError(required_message)\n                return []\n            frame = conn.CASTable(name, caslib=CASLIB).to_frame()\n            rows = []\n            for record in frame.to_dict(\"records\"):\n                row = {}\n                for key, value in record.items():\n                    row[str(key).lower()] = None if pd.isna(value) else value\n                rows.append(row)\n            return rows\n\n        def label_columns(name, columns):\n            \"\"\"Put the shipped column labels on a CAS table - they survive\n            the promote, so the pipeline tables read without the schema.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                from rag_core.steps import column_labels\n                labels = column_labels(columns)\n                if labels:\n                    conn.table.alterTable(\n                        caslib=CASLIB, name=name,\n                        columns=[{\"name\": column, \"label\": label}\n                                 for column, label in labels.items()])\n            except Exception as exc:\n                M(f\"column labels not applied to {name}: {exc}\")\n\n        def cas_stage(name, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n            \"\"\"Upload the session-scope staging table <name>_S with varchar\n            columns (no 32k limit); the SAS side swaps it into the promoted\n            global table and saves it, so the previous state survives a\n            mid-step failure.\"\"\"\n            if not rows:\n                return 0\n            data = []\n            for row in rows:\n                rec = []\n                for column in columns:\n                    value = row.get(column)\n                    if column in numeric:\n                        try:\n                            rec.append(float(value or 0))\n                        except Exception:\n                            rec.append(0.0)\n                    else:\n                        rec.append(\"\" if value is None else str(value))\n                data.append(rec)\n            frame = pd.DataFrame(data, columns=list(columns))\n            spec = [{\"name\": column,\n                     \"type\": \"double\" if column in numeric else \"varchar\"}\n                    for column in columns]\n            conn.upload_frame(frame,\n                              casout={\"name\": name + \"_S\", \"caslib\": CASLIB,\n                                      \"replace\": True},\n                              importoptions={\"fileType\": \"csv\",\n                                             \"allowEmbeddedNewLines\": True,\n                                             \"vars\": spec})\n            label_columns(name + \"_S\", columns)\n            return len(rows)\n\n        # ---- rag_core bootstrap: download the governed SAS Content folder --\n        def get_json(endpoint, **params):\n            response = requests.get(BASE + endpoint, params=params, headers=AUTH,\n                                    verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n            response.raise_for_status()\n            return response.json()\n\n        def download_folder(folder_id, local_dir):\n            os.makedirs(local_dir, exist_ok=True)\n            count = 0\n            members = get_json(f\"/folders/folders/{folder_id}/members\", limit=200)\n            for member in members.get(\"items\", []):\n                uri = member.get(\"uri\", \"\")\n                if \"/files/files/\" in uri:\n                    content = requests.get(BASE + uri + \"/content\", headers=AUTH,\n                                           verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 60))\n                    content.raise_for_status()\n                    with open(os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]), \"wb\") as fh:\n                        fh.write(content.content)\n                    count += 1\n                elif \"/folders/folders/\" in uri:\n                    count += download_folder(uri.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1],\n                                             os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]))\n            return count\n\n        core_path = (clean_path(P[\"_rgex_ragCorePath\"])\n                     or \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\")\n        root = requests.get(BASE + \"/folders/folders/@item\",\n                            params={\"path\": core_path}, headers=AUTH,\n                            verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n        if root.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"rag_core folder {core_path} not found \"\n                               f\"(HTTP {root.status_code}) - deploy it per the \"\n                               \"administration guide\")\n        staging = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"rag_core_\")\n        n_files = download_folder(root.json()[\"id\"], os.path.join(staging, \"rag_core\"))\n        sys.path.insert(0, staging)\n        import rag_core\n        M(f\"rag_core {rag_core.RAG_CORE_VERSION} bootstrapped ({n_files} files)\")\n\n        from rag_core.extractors import ExtractorRegistry\n        from rag_core.sources import reader_for\n        from rag_core.steps import (ELEMENT_COLUMNS, INVENTORY_COLUMNS,\n                                    run_extract, stamp_config)\n\n        inventory_columns = INVENTORY_COLUMNS\n        inventory = read_rows(\"rgex_inventory_in.json\",\n                              \"the inventory input port is not connected - \"\n                              \"wire the RAG - List Documents output into \"\n                              \"this step\")\n        registry = ExtractorRegistry()\n        catalog = registry.catalog()\n        unavailable = catalog[\"unavailable\"]\n        if unavailable:\n            M(f\"extractors unavailable (packages missing): {unavailable}\")\n\n        # documents keep their source: the step re-reads them where the List\n        # step found them, so no second folder has to be picked here\n        kinds = sorted({(row.get(\"source_kind\") or \"path\") for row in inventory\n                        if row.get(\"status\") in (\"new\", \"changed\")})\n        source = None\n        for kind in kinds:\n            source = source or reader_for(kind, BASE, TOKEN, VERIFY)\n        forced = P[\"_rgex_extractor\"]\n        if forced in (\"\", \"auto\"):\n            forced = None\n\n        elements, updated = run_extract(inventory, registry,\n                                        extractor_name=forced,\n                                        source=source, log=M)\n        n_elements = cas_stage(project_table(\"_ELEMENTS\"), elements,\n                               ELEMENT_COLUMNS, numeric=(\"level\", \"page\"))\n        stamp_config(updated, {\"extractor\": forced or \"auto\"})\n        n_inventory = write_rows(\"rgex_inventory_out.json\", stamp(updated),\n                                 inventory_columns, numeric=(\"chunk_count\",))\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_nel\", str(n_elements))\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_ninv\", str(n_inventory))\n        n_docs = sum(1 for r in updated\n                     if r.get(\"extractor\") and r.get(\"status\") != \"failed\")\n        n_failed = sum(1 for r in updated if r.get(\"status\") == \"failed\")\n        used = {}\n        for row in updated:\n            if row.get(\"extractor\") and row.get(\"status\") != \"failed\":\n                used[row[\"extractor\"]] = used.get(row[\"extractor\"], 0) + 1\n        summarize(\"extractor: \" + (forced or \"chosen per file format\"))\n        summarize(f\"sources read: {', '.join(kinds) or 'none pending'}\")\n        summarize(f\"{n_docs} documents extracted, {n_failed} failed, \"\n                  f\"{n_inventory - n_docs - n_failed} skipped as unchanged\")\n        if used:\n            summarize(\"extractors used: \"\n                      + \", \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in sorted(used.items())))\n        if unavailable:\n            summarize(f\"unavailable extractors: {', '.join(sorted(unavailable))}\")\n        summarize(f\"{n_elements} elements written to \"\n                  f\"{CASLIB}.{project_table('_ELEMENTS')}\")\n        publish_summary(\"_rgex_summary\")\n\n        try:\n            conn.close(close_session=False)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_rc\", \"0\")\n    except Exception as error:\n        error_text = f\"{type(error).__name__}: {error}\"\n        M(\"failed: \" + sas_safe(error_text))\n        print(traceback.format_exc())\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_error\", sas_safe(error_text)[:500])\n\n\nmain()\nendsubmit;\nrun; quit;\nproc python terminate;\nrun; quit;\n\n%macro _rgex_swap(suffix, count, persist=1);\n    %if &_rgex_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %if &count. LT 0 %then %return;\n    proc casutil sessref=rgexcas incaslib=\"&_rgex_tablesCaslib.\"\n                 outcaslib=\"&_rgex_tablesCaslib.\";\n        droptable casdata=\"&_rgex_ragProject.&suffix.\" quiet;\n        %if &count. GT 0 %then %do;\n            promote casdata=\"&_rgex_ragProject.&suffix._S\"\n                    casout=\"&_rgex_ragProject.&suffix.\";\n            %if &persist. EQ 1 %then %do;\n                save casdata=\"&_rgex_ragProject.&suffix.\"\n                     casout=\"&_rgex_ragProject.&suffix.\" replace;\n            %end;\n            %else %do;\n                /* not persisted by choice: clear any file an earlier run\n                   saved, or a restart would resurrect stale content */\n                deletesource casdata=\"&_rgex_ragProject.&suffix..sashdat\" quiet;\n            %end;\n        %end;\n        %else %do;\n            deletesource casdata=\"&_rgex_ragProject.&suffix..sashdat\" quiet;\n        %end;\n    quit;\n%mend _rgex_swap;\n%_rgex_swap(_ELEMENTS, &_rgex_nel., persist=&_rgex_persist.);\n%macro _rgex_passthrough;\n    %if &_rgex_state. NE skip %then %return;\n    %local lib table opts;\n    %let lib = %upcase(%scan(&_rgex_invout., 1, .));\n    %let table = %scan(&_rgex_invout., 2, .);\n    %if &lib. EQ %upcase(rgexout) %then %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rgexcas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgex_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgex_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&table.\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        %let opts = (promote=yes);\n    %end;\n    %else %let opts = (compress=yes);\n    %if %symexist(_rgex_inventory) %then\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgex_inventory)) NE 0 %then\n    %if %sysfunc(exist(&_rgex_inventory.)) %then %do;\n        data &_rgex_invout.&opts.;\n            set &_rgex_inventory.;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgex_passthrough;\n%_rgex_passthrough;\n\n%macro _rgex_emit_inventory;\n    %if &_rgex_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %local lib table opts;\n    %let lib = %upcase(%scan(&_rgex_invout., 1, .));\n    %let table = %scan(&_rgex_invout., 2, .);\n    %if &lib. EQ %upcase(rgexout) %then %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rgexcas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgex_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgex_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&table.\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        %let opts = (promote=yes);\n    %end;\n    %else %let opts = (compress=yes);\n    %if &_rgex_ninv. GT 0 %then %do;\n        filename rgexino \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/rgex_inventory_out.json\";\n        libname rgexinj json fileref=rgexino;\n        data &_rgex_invout.&opts.;\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n                   content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n                   pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n                   run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24 extractor $ 64\n                   rag_project $ 20 tables_caslib $ 32 config_json $ 1024;\n            label doc_id=\"Document ID\" source_uri=\"Source location\"\n                  source_kind=\"Source type\" content_hash=\"Content fingerprint\"\n                  mtime=\"Source last modified\" status=\"Ingestion status\"\n                  error_text=\"Failure reason\" pipeline_version=\"Pipeline version\"\n                  config_hash=\"Configuration fingerprint\" chunk_count=\"Chunks produced\"\n                  run_id=\"Ingestion run ID\" updated_at=\"Row updated (UTC)\"\n                  extractor=\"Text extractor used\" rag_project=\"RAG project\"\n                  tables_caslib=\"Pipeline tables caslib\"\n                  config_json=\"Pipeline configuration (JSON)\";\n            set rgexinj.root(drop=ordinal_root);\n        run;\n        libname rgexinj clear;\n        filename rgexino clear;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        data &_rgex_invout.&opts.;\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n                   content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n                   pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n                   run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24 extractor $ 64\n                   rag_project $ 20 tables_caslib $ 32 config_json $ 1024;\n            label doc_id=\"Document ID\" source_uri=\"Source location\"\n                  source_kind=\"Source type\" content_hash=\"Content fingerprint\"\n                  mtime=\"Source last modified\" status=\"Ingestion status\"\n                  error_text=\"Failure reason\" pipeline_version=\"Pipeline version\"\n                  config_hash=\"Configuration fingerprint\" chunk_count=\"Chunks produced\"\n                  run_id=\"Ingestion run ID\" updated_at=\"Row updated (UTC)\"\n                  extractor=\"Text extractor used\" rag_project=\"RAG project\"\n                  tables_caslib=\"Pipeline tables caslib\"\n                  config_json=\"Pipeline configuration (JSON)\";\n            call missing(of _all_);\n            stop;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgex_emit_inventory;\n%_rgex_emit_inventory;\n%macro _rgex_release;\n    %local failing;\n    %let failing = 0;\n    %if &_rgex_state. EQ fail %then %let failing = 1;\n    %if &_rgex_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgex_rc. NE 0 %then %let failing = 1;\n    %if &failing. EQ 0 %then %return;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgex_runId) %then %return;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgex_runId)) EQ 0 %then %return;\n    %if not %sysfunc(exist(rgexout.&_rgex_ragProject._LEDGER)) %then %return;\n    data rgexout.&_rgex_ragProject._LEDGER_R(replace=yes);\n        set rgexout.&_rgex_ragProject._LEDGER(where=(not (doc_id = \"__run_lock__\"\n                                 and run_id = \"&_rgex_runId.\")));\n    run;\n    proc casutil sessref=rgexcas incaslib=\"&_rgex_tablesCaslib.\"\n                 outcaslib=\"&_rgex_tablesCaslib.\";\n        droptable casdata=\"&_rgex_ragProject._LEDGER\" quiet;\n        promote casdata=\"&_rgex_ragProject._LEDGER_R\"\n                casout=\"&_rgex_ragProject._LEDGER\";\n        save casdata=\"&_rgex_ragProject._LEDGER\"\n             casout=\"&_rgex_ragProject._LEDGER\" replace;\n    quit;\n    data _null_;\n        putLog \"NOTE: RAG - Extract Text: the run lock was released so the run can be retried\";\n    run;\n%mend _rgex_release;\n%_rgex_release;\n\nlibname rgexout clear;\ncas rgexcas terminate;\n\n%macro _rgex_status;\n    %if &_rgex_state. EQ run %then %if &_rgex_rc. NE 0 %then\n        %let _rgex_state = fail;\n    %if &_rgex_state. EQ skip %then %do;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - Extract Text: skipped -----\";\n        run;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    %if &_rgex_state. EQ fail %then %do;\n        %let RAG_PIPELINE_FAILED = 1;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"ERROR: RAG - Extract Text failed: %superq(_rgex_error)\";\n        run;\n        %if &RAG_ABORT_ON_ERROR. NE 0 %then %do;\n            data _null_;\n                abort 42;\n            run;\n        %end;\n        %return;\n    %end;\n    data _null_;\n        length part $ 500;\n        putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - Extract Text -----\";\n        do i = 1 to countw(\"%superq(_rgex_summary)\", \"|\");\n            part = strip(scan(\"%superq(_rgex_summary)\", i, \"|\"));\n            if part ne \"\" then putLog \"NOTE:   \" part;\n        end;\n    run;\n%mend _rgex_status;\n%_rgex_status;"}, "type": "code", "ui": "{\n\t\"showPageContentOnly\": true,\n\t\"pages\": [\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageDefinition\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Definition\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_info\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Extracts text elements from every new or changed document in the inventory into the promoted CAS table <project>_ELEMENTS. Formats: plaintext, markdown, CSV/JSON, HTML and the PDF text layer (pypdfium2); markitdown formats when that package is installed. A corrupt document is marked failed and skipped - the flow keeps running.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_inventory\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"inputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Document inventory (from RAG - List Documents):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_extractor\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Text extractor:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"auto\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Automatic (by file extension)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"csv_json\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"csv_json (.csv, .json, .jsonl, .ndjson, .tsv)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"email\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"email (.eml, .mht, .mhtml)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"html\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"html (.htm, .html, .xhtml)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"markdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"markdown (.markdown, .md)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"markitdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"markitdown (.docx, .epub, .msg, .pptx, .rtf, .xlsx)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"pdf-text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"pdf-text (.pdf)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"plaintext\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"plaintext (.log, .text, .txt)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_sectionAdvanced\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Runtime\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_persist\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Element table (<project>_ELEMENTS):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"1\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Save to disk (survives a server restart)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"0\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Keep in memory only (rebuilt on the next run)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"path\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SAS Content folder holding rag_core (set by the deployment - not editable here):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"pathtype\": \"folder\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"enabled\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgex_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"__set_by_deployment__\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_invout\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"outputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Updated inventory output (wire this one forward):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageAbout\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"About\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textAbout\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"RAG - Extract Text step\\n==========\\n\\nRe-reads the bytes of every new or changed document and runs the rag_core extractor registry. Elements land in <project>_ELEMENTS (promoted + saved); when no documents are pending the table is removed - an absent table is the pipeline's empty state. Documents whose extraction fails are marked failed in the updated inventory and retry on the next run.\\n\\nFlow wiring: chain the document INVENTORY through every step - RAG - List Documents \u2192 Extract Text \u2192 Chunk Documents \u2192 Embed Chunks \u2192 Load Vector Store. The bulk data travels beside the flow in promoted CAS tables named <project>_ELEMENTS, <project>_CHUNKS, <project>_EMBEDDED and <project>_LEDGER in the tables caslib (each saved to disk, so state survives server restarts; names stay within 32 characters so they display nicely in SAS Studio). Each step's output table lands in that same caslib as <project>_INV_LIST, _INV_EXTRACT, _INV_CHUNK, _INV_EMBED and <project>_LOAD_REPORT unless you point the output port somewhere else. Give every step the SAME project name and caslib.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Pre-requisites\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Tested on SAS Viya 2026 (Stable).\\n\\n* The rag_core runtime must be deployed to SAS Content (default: /SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core) with deploy-rag-content.ps1/.sh - keep that folder read-only for regular users.\\n* The compute context's Python needs the requests, swat and pandas packages (swat/pandas carry the pipeline tables to CAS - varchar columns, no 32k limit).\\n* CAS available; the runner needs write access to the tables caslib.\\n* pypdfium2 for the PDF text layer, markitdown for Office formats (each optional - matching extractors deactivate when a package is missing).\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Changelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"* Version: 1.2 (29JUL2026)\\n      - SAS Content document sources; output tables land in the tables caslib; labelled columns; numeric and list-of-values fields; run summary in the log\\n* Version: 1.1 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Pipeline tables move to promoted CAS tables via SWAT (varchar, no 32k limit); automatic embed checkpoint\\n* Version: 1.0 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Initial version\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t}\n\t],\n\t\"syntaxversion\": \"1.3.0\",\n\t\"values\": {\n\t\t\"_rgex_ragCorePath\": \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\",\n\t\t\"_rgex_persist\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"1\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Save to disk (survives a server restart)\"\n\t\t},\n\t\t\"_rgex_extractor\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"auto\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Automatic (by file extension)\"\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}"}